From 0610e2b1c65459569069d681eb4d9d56c5c5dad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:36:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): measure the cross drill about the work offset's
 spindle

The radial kernel measured every standoff (bar radius, station side,
hop/clearance radii, the station-change chord law) about world Z through
world (0, 0), while the posts program about world Z through the work
offset's origin. A bar moved off the world origin with G54 moved onto
it drilled a different chain from G54 than the same bar on the origin
(hop 26.444/32.444/46.444 mm vs 21.213, final clearance 35.770 vs 15).

- operation/cross_spindle.rs: shift the holes into the spindle frame by
  the wcs_context origin (collected once as GenJob::wcs_origin), measure
  stock_r about that line, run the kernel, shift the chain back. An
  origin on world Z runs the kernel untouched (on-origin bits unchanged).
- spindle_law::turns also covers a mill-turn's cross drill, so a revolved
  bar off its work offset is refused by name there too.
- A plain lathe's cross drill refuses by name a part the axis fit cannot
  read as turned (the mill-turn keeps drilling prismatic bars).

Fixes #67

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
